  "verbalization": "Notoamide B is implicated in the regulation of Ataxin-2 through a series of molecular interactions that involve multiple targets. The evidence suggests that Notoamide B acts as a target for two distinct compounds: Malme-3M and Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, both of which are themselves targets of the compound Linustatin. This indicates a potential pathway where Notoamide B may influence the activity of these compounds, which in turn affect Ataxin-2. The shared involvement of Ataxin-2 in these pathways suggests a possible role in the biological processes that these compounds target. The consistent scores across the three paths, with a final score of 0.6489, support a plausible mechanistic link between Notoamide B and Ataxin-2, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
